From f5bc873c9a40c4d321d5c62c0ddc6fb1343eaba3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CosmosEx Buildroot <4372835+planeturban@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:12:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ce_main_app: image library: extended JSON lists, list and
 picture passthrough

Floppy library stage 6.3, app side (cosmosex-floppy-library.md 3a):

- A list whose first byte is '{' is an extended list (format
  "cosmosex-imagelist", format_version 1): entries with an id, a title,
  games (strings or objects) and any number of disks; each disk becomes
  an image in the library, with the entry's id and title, its number and
  label. Paths in "file" / "src": relative (no "..", no absolute paths,
  no other schemes); http(s) URLs in web lists only; relative paths are
  resolved against base_url or the list URL's folder (web) or the source
  folder (share/usb/local). Bad entries (no or duplicate id, no title, no
  disks) are skipped with a log line; at most 32 disks per entry, 64 MB
  per list. Inline pictures are not kept (the browser decodes them from
  the list); "src" pictures are kept per entry in document order. A
  folder's imagelist.json is used before its imagelist.csv. Legacy CSV
  items get an entry id (the image name) and a title (the first game).
- GET /api/v1/lists/<sourceId>: the source's list file as it is, with an
  ETag (size and time) and 304 on If-None-Match, Cache-Control no-cache.
- GET /api/v1/media/<sourceId>/<entryId>/<n>: picture n of an entry: a
  file in the source folder (realpath inside the folder) or fetched from
  the web list's server (http/https only, 3 redirects, 5 s, 256 KB), sent
  only if its first bytes are PNG, JPEG, WebP or GIF, with that type and
  nosniff. The request never carries a path or URL. Fetched without the
  image list lock held.
- Library search results: entryId, title, disk {index, count, label};
  sources: format (json / csv / scan).
